 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have departed\nLike stars; but all are fair to me above.\nWho would ask what manner of sorrow\nHath worn them down? - Or why should I lament\nFor some one's death that he had been happy?\nII. A splendid image hath died again,\nThe blue eye which on such suns did command;\nIt was a wonder if that vision\nShould leave our soul till twilight to\nO'erhang it in silence and decay.  Precision!\nIII. Alas, they must depart into",
